  "title": "Ukraine and Russia: Zelensky and Trump’s Strategic Dynamics Amid Starlink and Energy Deals",
  "summary": "Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky has criticized the U.S.-Russia diesel deal as a 'gift to Putin' while President Donald Trump defends the deal as a necessary step to secure energy supplies, amid growing tensions over Ukraine's military access to Starlink satellite internet. The Ukrainian leader accused the U.S. of picking the other side after four years of conflict.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine President Volodymyr Zelensky criticized the U.S.-Russia diesel deal as a 'gift to Putin', while U.S. President Donald Trump defended the deal as a necessary step to reduce fuel prices and secure supplies.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The deal comes ahead of upcoming US midterm elections in a context of rising fuel costs.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Ukraine's military access to Starlink satellite internet terminals was temporarily restricted due to US pressure to halt Russian long-range strikes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
